<tool id="genomecov_coverage_table" name="Genome coverage table" version="@TOOL_VERSION@+galaxy@VERSION_SUFFIX@" profile="@PROFILE@" license="MIT">
    <description>from bedtools genomecov histograms</description>
    <macros>
        <import>macros.xml</import>
    </macros>
    <expand macro="requirements"/>
    <required_files>
        <include path="genomecov_coverage_table.py"/>
    </required_files>
    <version_command>python3 '$__tool_directory__/genomecov_coverage_table.py' --version</version_command>
    <command detect_errors="aggressive"><![CDATA[
python3 '$__tool_directory__/genomecov_coverage_table.py'
    --config '$config'
    --min-depth $min_depth
    --decimals $decimals
    --output '$output'
    ]]></command>
    <configfiles>
        <configfile name="config"><![CDATA[#import json
#set $config_columns = []
#for $column in $columns
    #set $histograms = []
    #for $element in $column.histograms
        #silent $histograms.append({"identifier": str($element.element_identifier), "path": str($element)})
    #end for
    #silent $config_columns.append({"label": str($column.label), "histograms": $histograms})
#end for
#echo json.dumps($config_columns)
]]></configfile>
    </configfiles>
    <inputs>
        <repeat name="columns" title="Column" min="1">
            <param name="label" type="text" label="Column label" help="Header of this column, for example the name of the masker. Each label must be unique.">
                <sanitizer invalid_char="">
                    <valid initial="string.printable">
                        <remove value="&#9;"/>
                        <remove value="&#10;"/>
                        <remove value="&#13;"/>
                    </valid>
                </sanitizer>
                <validator type="regex" message="Enter a label without tabs or line breaks">^[^\t\n\r]*\S[^\t\n\r]*$</validator>
            </param>
            <param name="histograms" type="data_collection" collection_type="list" format="tabular" label="bedtools genomecov histograms" help="One histogram for each sample. The element identifier is the sample name."/>
        </repeat>
        <param argument="--min-depth" type="integer" min="1" value="1" label="Minimum depth" help="Count a base as covered when its depth is at least this value"/>
        <param argument="--decimals" type="integer" min="0" max="10" value="2" label="Decimal places"/>
    </inputs>
    <outputs>
        <data name="output" format="tabular" label="${tool.name} on ${on_string}"/>
    </outputs>
    <tests>
        <!-- Masking workflow case: genomecov -max 1, defaults; byte-identical to masking_table -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="1">
            <repeat name="columns">
                <param name="label" value="dustmasker"/>
                <param name="histograms">
                    <collection type="list">
                        <element name="cs10_A" value="dustmasker_cs10_A.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                        <element name="cs10_B" value="dustmasker_cs10_B.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                    </collection>
                </param>
            </repeat>
            <repeat name="columns">
                <param name="label" value="windowmasker"/>
                <param name="histograms">
                    <collection type="list">
                        <element name="cs10_A" value="windowmasker_cs10_A.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                        <element name="cs10_B" value="windowmasker_cs10_B.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                    </collection>
                </param>
            </repeat>
            <repeat name="columns">
                <param name="label" value="tantan"/>
                <param name="histograms">
                    <collection type="list">
                        <element name="cs10_A" value="tantan_cs10_A.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                        <element name="cs10_B" value="tantan_cs10_B.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                    </collection>
                </param>
            </repeat>
            <repeat name="columns">
                <param name="label" value="fastan"/>
                <param name="histograms">
                    <collection type="list">
                        <element name="cs10_A" value="fastan_cs10_A.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                        <element name="cs10_B" value="fastan_cs10_B.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                    </collection>
                </param>
            </repeat>
            <repeat name="columns">
                <param name="label" value="union"/>
                <param name="histograms">
                    <collection type="list">
                        <element name="cs10_A" value="union_cs10_A.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                        <element name="cs10_B" value="union_cs10_B.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                    </collection>
                </param>
            </repeat>
            <output name="output" file="masking_workflow.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
        </test>
        <!-- Columns follow the repeat order, values follow labels, rows follow the first collection -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="1">
            <repeat name="columns">
                <param name="label" value="union"/>
                <param name="histograms">
                    <collection type="list">
                        <element name="cs10_B" value="union_cs10_B.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                        <element name="cs10_A" value="union_cs10_A.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                    </collection>
                </param>
            </repeat>
            <repeat name="columns">
                <param name="label" value="dustmasker"/>
                <param name="histograms">
                    <collection type="list">
                        <element name="cs10_A" value="dustmasker_cs10_A.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                        <element name="cs10_B" value="dustmasker_cs10_B.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                    </collection>
                </param>
            </repeat>
            <repeat name="columns">
                <param name="label" value="fastan"/>
                <param name="histograms">
                    <collection type="list">
                        <element name="cs10_A" value="fastan_cs10_A.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                        <element name="cs10_B" value="fastan_cs10_B.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                    </collection>
                </param>
            </repeat>
            <output name="output" ftype="tabular">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_n_lines n="3"/>
                    <has_line_matching expression="^Sample\tunion\tdustmasker\tfastan$"/>
                    <has_line_matching expression="^cs10_B\t7\.85\t3\.55\t0\.00$"/>
                    <has_line_matching expression="^cs10_A\t21\.41\t12\.26\t9\.24$"/>
                    <has_text_matching expression="^Sample[^\n]*\ncs10_B\t"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- Histogram without -max: depth 1, 2 and 3 rows are summed -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="1">
            <repeat name="columns">
                <param name="label" value="multi_depth"/>
                <param name="histograms">
                    <collection type="list">
                        <element name="s1" value="nomax_s1.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                        <element name="s2" value="nomax_s2.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                    </collection>
                </param>
            </repeat>
            <output name="output" ftype="tabular">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_n_lines n="3"/>
                    <has_line line="Sample&#9;multi_depth"/>
                    <has_line line="s1&#9;26.67"/>
                    <has_line line="s2&#9;24.00"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- Minimum depth 2 and 3 decimal places -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="1">
            <repeat name="columns">
                <param name="label" value="multi_depth"/>
                <param name="histograms">
                    <collection type="list">
                        <element name="s1" value="nomax_s1.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                        <element name="s2" value="nomax_s2.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                    </collection>
                </param>
            </repeat>
            <param name="min_depth" value="2"/>
            <param name="decimals" value="3"/>
            <output name="output" ftype="tabular">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_n_lines n="3"/>
                    <has_line line="Sample&#9;multi_depth"/>
                    <has_line line="s1&#9;7.333"/>
                    <has_line line="s2&#9;3.333"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- A column without a depth 2 row reports 0 -->
        <test expect_num_outputs="1">
            <repeat name="columns">
                <param name="label" value="dustmasker"/>
                <param name="histograms">
                    <collection type="list">
                        <element name="cs10_A" value="dustmasker_cs10_A.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                        <element name="cs10_B" value="dustmasker_cs10_B.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                    </collection>
                </param>
            </repeat>
            <param name="min_depth" value="2"/>
            <param name="decimals" value="3"/>
            <output name="output" ftype="tabular">
                <assert_contents>
                    <has_line line="Sample&#9;dustmasker"/>
                    <has_line line="cs10_A&#9;0.000"/>
                    <has_line line="cs10_B&#9;0.000"/>
                </assert_contents>
            </output>
        </test>
        <!-- Columns with different identifiers fail -->
        <test expect_failure="true" expect_exit_code="1">
            <repeat name="columns">
                <param name="label" value="dustmasker"/>
                <param name="histograms">
                    <collection type="list">
                        <element name="cs10_A" value="dustmasker_cs10_A.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                        <element name="cs10_B" value="dustmasker_cs10_B.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                    </collection>
                </param>
            </repeat>
            <repeat name="columns">
                <param name="label" value="fastan"/>
                <param name="histograms">
                    <collection type="list">
                        <element name="cs10_A" value="fastan_cs10_A.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                    </collection>
                </param>
            </repeat>
            <assert_stderr>
                <has_text text="column 'fastan' identifiers differ from column 'dustmasker': missing cs10_B; extra none"/>
            </assert_stderr>
        </test>
        <!-- Duplicate labels fail -->
        <test expect_failure="true" expect_exit_code="1">
            <repeat name="columns">
                <param name="label" value="dustmasker"/>
                <param name="histograms">
                    <collection type="list">
                        <element name="cs10_A" value="dustmasker_cs10_A.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                        <element name="cs10_B" value="dustmasker_cs10_B.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                    </collection>
                </param>
            </repeat>
            <repeat name="columns">
                <param name="label" value="dustmasker"/>
                <param name="histograms">
                    <collection type="list">
                        <element name="cs10_A" value="dustmasker_cs10_A.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                        <element name="cs10_B" value="dustmasker_cs10_B.genomecov.tabular" ftype="tabular"/>
                    </collection>
                </param>
            </repeat>
            <assert_stderr>
                <has_text text="duplicate column label 'dustmasker'"/>
            </assert_stderr>
        </test>
    </tests>
    <help format="markdown"><![CDATA[
**What it does**

This tool combines `bedtools genomecov` histograms into one table. Each value is the percent of a sample's genome with a depth of at least the minimum depth.

-----

**Inputs**

Add one column for each set of histograms. Each column has:

- A label. The label is the column header. Each label must be unique and cannot contain tabs or line breaks.
- A list collection of `bedtools genomecov` histograms (the default output, not `-d`, `-bg` or `-bga`). The collection has one histogram for each sample. The element identifier is the sample name.

All columns must have the same sample names. If a column has a missing or extra sample, the tool stops. The error names the column and the samples.

-----

**Calculation**

The tool reads the `genome` rows of each histogram. These rows have 5 columns: `genome`, depth, bases at that depth, genome size, and the fraction of the genome at that depth.

The tool adds the fractions of the rows with a depth of at least the minimum depth. Then it multiplies the sum by 100. It rounds the result to the number of decimal places that you set. If no `genome` row has a depth of at least the minimum depth, the value is 0. If a histogram has no `genome` rows, the tool stops with an error.

`bedtools genomecov -max N` puts all depths of N or more in the row for depth N. For this output, set a minimum depth of N or less. With `-max 1` and the default minimum depth of 1, each value is the percent of the genome that the intervals cover. An example is the percent of the genome that a repeat masker masked.

-----

**Output**

The output is a tabular file. The header is `Sample`, then the labels in the order of the columns. The table has one row for each sample, in the order of the first column's collection. The header has no leading `#`, so MultiQC custom content can read the file as a table.

```
Sample	dustmasker	windowmasker
cs10_A	12.26	10.52
cs10_B	3.55	1.01
```
    ]]></help>
    <expand macro="citations"/>
</tool>
